<h1 class="text-darkgreen">College Majors Ranked by Earnings vs. Debt</h1>
<h4 class="text-green"><%= field_rank_heading(@ranking) %>, for bachelor's degrees</h4>
<p class="text-green">Costs for families earning <%= income_bracket_label(@income) %> a year</p>

<section class="mt-4 max-w-3xl space-y-2 text-base leading-6 text-gray-900">
  <p>
    Months to repay is how many months of first-year pay it takes to clear the typical student loan. Years of pay is how many years of first-year pay the full four-year cost takes.
    Lower is better for both. <a href="#how-we-figure" class="text-green">How we figure these</a>.
  </p>
  <%= if grad_school_note?(@ranking) do %>
    <p class="grad-school-note text-sm text-gray-900 bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-400 px-3 py-2">
      Majors that lead to graduate school, like communication disorders or pre-physical therapy, show low first-year pay because many graduates are still in school.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</section>

<section class="w-full pb-8 pt-8">
  <%= form_for @conn, Routes.field_path(@conn, :rank), [method: :get, class: "flex flex-wrap items-end gap-x-8 gap-y-4"], fn f -> %>
    <div class="max-w-full">
      <label for="rank_select" class="block text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-green">Ranking</label>
      <%= select f, :rank, field_rank_views(), id: "rank_select", value: @ranking, onchange: "this.form.submit()", class: "form-input pl-2 pr-8 sm:text-sm sm:leading-5 max-w-full" %>
    </div>
    <div class="max-w-full">
      <label for="income_select" class="block text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-green">Family income</label>
      <%= select f, :income, income_bracket_options(), id: "income_select", value: @income, onchange: "this.form.submit()", class: "form-input pl-2 pr-8 sm:text-sm sm:leading-5 max-w-full" %>
    </div>
    <div>
      <label for="count_select" class="block text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-green">Count</label>
      <%= select f, :count, @rank_counts, id: "count_select", value: @count, onchange: "this.form.submit()", class: "form-input pl-6 pr-8 sm:text-sm sm:leading-5" %>
    </div>
    <%= if @ranking in ["top_earnings", "bottom_earnings"] do %>
      <div class="pb-1">
        <label class="inline-flex items-center text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-green cursor-pointer">
          <%= checkbox f, :require_debt, value: @require_debt, onchange: "this.form.submit()", class: "form-checkbox mr-2" %>
          Only show majors that report debt
        </label>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</section>

<section>
  <% diff_data = Poison.encode!(field_chart_data(@ranks)) %>
  <%= raw Chartkick.column_chart diff_data, prefix: "$", width: "100%", title: "What's Worth It?", colors: ["#114b5f", "#1a93df", "#88d498"], library: %{
      scales: %{
        xAxes: [%{
          ticks: %{
            display: false
          },
          gridLines: %{
            display: false
          }
        }]
      }
    }
  %>
</section>

<table class="rank-table md:block lg:table pt-8 table-auto">
  <thead class="md:absolute md:-top-9999 md:-left-9999">
    <tr>
      <.header label="College Name" tooltip_key="name" />
      <.header label="Field" tooltip_key="field" />
      <.header label="Admissions Rate" tooltip_key="admissions" />
      <.header label="4-Year Cost" tooltip_key="cost4" />
      <.header label="Debt" tooltip="The median federal student-loan debt of graduates of this major who borrowed. Parent PLUS loans are not included." />
      <.header label={humanize_header("Field Earnings")} tooltip="Median earnings 1 year after graduation for this major at this college" />
      <.header label="Months to Repay" tooltip_key="months" />
      <.header label="Years of Pay" tooltip_key="value_years" />
    </tr>
  </thead>

  <tbody class="md:block">
    <%= for rank <- @ranks do %>
      <tr class="md:block odd:bg-gray-50">
        <td class="px-4 py-3 college-field md:border-none md:relative md:block xl:text-sm whitespace-wrap border-b text-green"><%= link shorten(rank.college_name), to: Routes.college_path(@conn, :show, rank.unit_id, rank.college_name) %> </td>
        <td class="px-4 py-3 field-field md:border-none md:relative md:block xl:text-sm  whitespace-wrap border-b text-green"><%= link field_short_name(rank.field_name), to: field_page_path(rank.field_name)%> </td>
        <td class="px-4 py-3 admissions-field md:border-none md:relative md:block xl:text-sm  whitespace-wrap border-b ">
          <%= percent(rank.admissions) %>
          <%= if is_number(rank.sat_avg) and rank.sat_avg > 0 do %>
            <div class="text-xs text-gray-600">Avg SAT <%= rank.sat_avg %></div>
          <% end %>
        </td>
        <.cost_cell net_price={rank.net_price} sticker={rank.sticker} debt={rank.cost} />
        <td class="px-4 py-3 cost-field md:border-none md:relative md:block xl:text-sm whitespace-nowrap border-b">
          <%= if no_data?(rank.cost) do %>
            <span class="text-gray-400 italic">N/A</span>
          <% else %>
            <%= cash(rank.cost) %>
          <% end %>
        </td>

        <td class={"px-4 py-3 earnings-field md:border-none md:relative md:block xl:text-sm #{if @ranking == "top_earnings" || @ranking == "bottom_earnings", do: "font-bold", else: ""} whitespace-wrap border-b "}><%= cash(rank.payoff) %></td>

        <.months_cell value={rank.months} parent_debt={rank.parent_debt} earnings={rank.payoff} />
        <.years_cell value={rank.value_years} bold={@ranking in ["best_value", "worst_value"]} />

      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<section id="how-we-figure" class="pt-12 text-gray-700 space-y-4 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="text-xl text-darkgreen">How we figure these</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Months to repay</strong> divides a program's median federal student-loan debt by one month of its graduates' median pay in their first year.
    At 6 months, the typical borrower owes about half a year's pay. It uses gross pay, before taxes, rent and other bills, so paying the loans off really takes longer.
    It counts only graduates who borrowed, and leaves out loans their parents took. Programs that don't report their debt aren't ranked.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Parent loans.</strong> When parents who took Parent PLUS loans owed more than <%= parent_plus_warning_months() %> months of their child's first-year pay, a note shows that figure on its own.
    We never add it to the student's debt.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Four-year cost</strong> is a year's cost after grants, times four. It includes housing, food and books.
    It is the average for aided first-time full-time students in the family income bracket you pick, reported for the whole school rather than each major.
    It assumes you finish in four years. Families who get no aid pay closer to the sticker price, shown beneath it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>The gap</strong> is the four-year cost minus the median federal student loan. A family covers it from savings, work, Parent PLUS or private loans.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Years of pay</strong> divides the four-year cost by a year of first-year pay. At 2.0 years, the degree costs two years of a graduate's first-year pay.
  </p>
  <p>
    All data comes from the U.S. Department of Education's College Scorecard.
  </p>
</section>
